LOCATION:Skopelos Town\, Skopelos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 5 August the 16th-century monastery of Metamorfosi tou Sotiros above the Chora holds festive vespers with artoklasia at 8 pm\, often with Athonite monks concelebrating\, and the liturgy at 7.30 next morning. On the evening of the 6th the Dimos Skopelou stages the town's big open-air panigiri on the harbour front / KAPI courtyard with a name nisiotika singer (Nasia Konitopoulou in 2025)\, free to attend. Go up to the monastery for the vespers and come down to the port for the dancing.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skopelos/#skopelos-town-panigiri-of-sotiros-transfiguration-skopelos-t
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skopelos/#skopelos-town-panigiri-of-sotiros-transfiguration-skopelos-t
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skopelos-glossa-loutraki-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-glossa-and-lou-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia (15 August)\, Glossa and Loutraki
LOCATION:Glossa / Loutraki\, Skopelos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The north of the island celebrates Dekapentavgoustos twice over: the municipality's panigiri on the little harbour of Loutraki (15 August in 2025\, the 16th in 2026\, with a local singer and dancing by the water)\, and since 2025 a revived all-night glenti in the central square of Glossa village above it\, where the music went on until 6 am. Between them there is a shuttle-worthy 3 km of hairpins\, so decide where you will sleep\; rooms in Glossa are few and go early in August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skopelos/#glossa-loutraki-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-glossa-and-lou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skopelos/#glossa-loutraki-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-glossa-and-lou
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skopelos-glossa-loutraki-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-glossa-and-lou-2028@aegeanblueprint.com
